 {
  "id": "ukmt-pink-2019-24",
  "bank": "ukmt",
  "source": {
   "contest": "UKMT Pink Kangaroo",
   "paper": "2019",
   "year": 2019,
   "number": 24,
   "url": "https://ukmt.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/pink-2019-q.pdf"
  },
  "grade": "9-10",
  "points": 6,
  "blankPoints": null,
  "wrongPoints": null,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "The diagram shows triangle $JKL$ of area $S$. The point $M$ is the midpoint of $KL$. The points $P$, $Q$, $R$ lie on the extended lines $LJ$, $MJ$, $KJ$, respectively, such that $JP=2\\times JL$, $JQ=3\\times JM$ and $JR=4\\times JK$. What is the area of triangle $PQR$?",
  "image": "qimages/ukmt/pink-2019/q24.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$S$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$2S$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$3S$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$\\frac12S$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$\\frac13S$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Compare areas using $\\frac12ab\\sin C$",
    "body": "Let $u$ be the area of $JLM$ and $v$ the area of $JMK$. Since $M$ is the midpoint of $KL$, $u=v=\\frac12S$.\n\n$\\angle QJR=\\angle KJM$ (vertically opposite) with $JR=4JK$ and $JQ=3JM$, so area $JQR=3\\times4\\times v=6S$. Similarly area $PJQ=2\\times3\\times u=3S$ and area $JPR=2\\times4\\times S=8S$.\n\nThe point $J$ lies outside triangle $PQR$, and triangles $PJQ$ and $JQR$ have the same orientation as $PQR$ while $JRP$ has the opposite one. So $[PQR]=[PJQ]+[JQR]-[JRP]=3S+6S-8S=S$.\n\n**Answer: (A) $S$**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Coordinates with vectors",
    "body": "Put $J$ at the origin, $K=\\mathbf k$, $L=\\mathbf l$, so $S=\\frac12|\\mathbf k\\times\\mathbf l|$. Then $P=-2\\mathbf l$, $Q=-\\frac32(\\mathbf k+\\mathbf l)$, $R=-4\\mathbf k$.\n\n$Q-P=-\\frac32\\mathbf k+\\frac12\\mathbf l$ and $R-P=-4\\mathbf k+2\\mathbf l$, so $(Q-P)\\times(R-P)=-3\\,\\mathbf k\\times\\mathbf l+2\\,\\mathbf k\\times\\mathbf l=-\\mathbf k\\times\\mathbf l$.\n\nHence $[PQR]=\\frac12|\\mathbf k\\times\\mathbf l|=S$.\n\n**Answer: (A) $S$**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "geometry"
  ],
